    <item>
      <title>automatic secure backup on usb with Luks/Udev</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/2023-10-08-automatic-usb-backup/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 08 Oct 2023 15:27:34 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2023-10-08-automatic-usb-backup/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The goal is to automatically mount a specific encrypted usb device on plugin, run a backup and umount it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;minor-goals&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Minor goals&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#minor-goals&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;simple and use standard linux tooling&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;do not break security&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;interactive, give user feedback&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;robust to interuptions&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;prerequisites&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Prerequisites&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#prerequisites&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;have a spare usb device&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;have root access&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;steps&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Steps&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#steps&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Prepare the encrypted usb device&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Setup automounting&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Setup automatic backup as root with visual feedback for an ordinary user&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;1-prepare-the-encrypted-usb-device&#34;&gt;&#xA;  1. Prepare the encrypted usb device&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#1-prepare-the-encrypted-usb-device&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Encrypt the device with &lt;a href=&#34;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_Unified_Key_Setup&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;luks&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>sleuth valve for tomcat</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/2017-11-26-inject-sleuth-header-on-first-request-with-tomcat/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 26 Nov 2017 14:00:07 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2017-11-26-inject-sleuth-header-on-first-request-with-tomcat/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;At &lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;idealo&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt; we do a lot of microservices with spring-boot.&#xA;To trace request we use &lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;spring-cloud-sleuth&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt; as &lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;opentracing&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt; implementation.&#xA;I&amp;rsquo;m missing the injection of the trace header on the first request. You still need to deliver those with your request. So here follows my solution…&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;concept&#34;&gt;&#xA;  concept&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#concept&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let me show my approach. It is aimed to be easy to implement and easy to comprehend.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>testing dockerfiles</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/2017-02-24-pragmatic-approach-to-add-tests-for-docker-files/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 23 Feb 2017 23:23:07 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2017-02-24-pragmatic-approach-to-add-tests-for-docker-files/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Since a while I&amp;rsquo;m facing regularly issues with images create from docker files.&#xA;So I&amp;rsquo;m trying to develop a simple approach to test them. It is inspired basically by&#xA;&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;TDD&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;concept&#34;&gt;&#xA;  concept&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#concept&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let me show my approach. It is aimed to be easy to implement and easy to comprehend.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I follow these simple steps:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;creating a &lt;code&gt;Dockerfile&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;create a &lt;code&gt;test.sh&lt;/code&gt; under &lt;code&gt;test/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;run &lt;code&gt;test.sh&lt;/code&gt; from &lt;code&gt;test/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;trivial-example&#34;&gt;&#xA;  trivial example&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#trivial-example&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Dockerfile&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>maven central release with github in 30 seconds</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/2016-09-21-maven-release-on-github-with-travisci/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Sep 2016 14:23:07 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/2016-09-21-maven-release-on-github-with-travisci/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;As a passionate developer I always strive to optimise my build chain for speed and simplicity. In this example I&amp;rsquo;d like to publish a library on &lt;a href=&#34;http://search.maven.org/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;maven central&lt;/a&gt; without any onsite build tooling except my IDE. So lets see how to get rid of gpg key management and implement a trivial &lt;em&gt;push-button release process&lt;/em&gt; with &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/lkwg82&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Github&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;https://travis-ci.org&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;TravisCI&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;(This is reblogged originally from &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/idealo/logback-redis/wiki/Release-Process&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;idealo/logback-redis/wiki/Release-Process&lt;/a&gt; and sponsored by &lt;a href=&#34;https:/www.idealo.de&#34; &gt;Idealo&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
